      "content": "From a purely deterministic standpoint focused solely on minimizing physical advantages, biological sex is the measurable factor that directly correlates with known physiological differences in performance. In this narrow, quantifiable frame of competitive advantage, prioritizing biological reality provides the clearest definition of fairness. However, logic also dictates that the definition of \"fairness\" itself is multifaceted, encompassing not only equal competitive opportunity but also social equity. Therefore, stating that one physical reality outweighs all other considerations is a prioritization, not a universal logical conclusion.",
