      "content": "but you're basically saying they're just different \"prioritizations.\" one is based on measurable, empirical data (biology) and the other is based on subjective feelings (identity). if we're talking about sports, which is a physical contest, shouldn't the empirical data take precedence? it seems like you're giving \"social equity\" the same weight as physical reality, even though they aren't even in the same category. isn't it actually less logical to treat them as equals in a sporting context?",
